    "checks": [
      "The RPC cutover keeps existing direct-message rows, including the legacy unattributed row.",
      "A second PostgreSQL session waits on an uncommitted block and then refuses the held send. Both reads and unread counts reflect the block.",
      "When a send locks first, the later block preserves that accepted row and hides it from both participants. Writes refuse a stale transaction snapshot.",
      "Unblocking only changes the caller\u2019s block. Exact replay is safe, and the opposite active block still protects the conversation.",
      "The isolated restore preserves private blocks, old history, exact retry and the raw-table access denial."
